{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279128-using-reality-zones-examples","id":1279128,"title":"Using Reality Zones, Examples?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-01-06T22:35:19-08:00","id":1279128,"title":"Using Reality Zones, Examples?","content":"I'm looking to introduce reality zones into my chronicle but I haven't really seen them deployed before. Has anyone implemented them beyond a simple technocratic/mystic contrast? How do STs take local beliefs into account without being either wildly reductive or over homogenizing the world?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/15603-phillycuriosity","name":"PhillyCuriosity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar15603_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T10:46:20-08:00","id":1279255,"title":"","content":"Well, one of the first things to remember is that Reality Zones don\u2019t have a set size. The Sanctum of a mage is basically a very small, very deliberately tailored reality zones.<br /> <br /> Thus, a faith healer\u2019s tent or a Victorian themed opium den could all be reality zones where certain phenomena become coincidental; miraculous cures (particularly of conditions like cancer or chronic pain) in the faith healer\u2019s tent or prophetic visions while soaking in the opium fumes.<br /> <br /> The other way to invoke reality zones would be when you\u2019re going far from the beaten path. When you\u2019re in the middle of the Amazon the tribal practices of invoking the ancestors or animal spirits to bring about a successful hunt or general good fortune actually produce tangible results in defiance of what the modern world says is probable.<br /> <br /> The main thing you have to do is research the folklore of the locals and essentially anything that lines up with that becomes coincidental. To take a common superstition as an example, in the right place casting a curse upon someone who spilled salt and didn\u2019t immediately throw some over their shoulder would be completely coincidental because the locals believe not doing so brings bad luck and your spell works with the reality zone\u2019s paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-07T19:13:17-08:00","id":1279370,"title":"","content":"There's a subtle form of Reality Zone when you go from urban environments into rural areas. In these places, people expect technology to not work so well, on account of being 1) situated in places with outdated infrastructure, 2) prone to have technology that is years or even decades out of date, and 3) what tech that IS &quot;new&quot; tends to be on the cheap side, on account of rural people tending to work under tighter financial constraints.<br /> <br /> What this means is that the residents - the ones who form the local Consensus - are accustomed to technology not working in an optimal manner. Even outsiders will carry on that expectation, because of their stereotyped impression of rural areas. As such, this Reality Zone will exhibit a bias against technomancy, especially when it comes to telecomms technology. So mages of Iteration X and the Virtual Adepts will find themselves working at a disadvantage. However, there's an argument to be made about certain &quot;DIY&quot; tech being functional, since rural folk of a mechanical bent make do with what they have. So while the sleek, &quot;iPod&quot; technology might suffer, an Etherite's weird science inventions, built in a garage out of salvaged parts, might edge out the competition.<br /> <br /> In any event, this sort of Reality Zone will also make easier those Effects that disrupt technology. As already stated, rural folk are accustomed to technology being inconsistent and finicky. They also tend to develop their own &quot;tricks&quot; for getting technology to work right, like slapping devices or twiddling with antenna. Whatever works (or they convince themselves works, through Confirmation Bias) will become ingrained, and thus become part of the local Consensus.<br /> <br /> Heck, I vaguely recall mentions in the Mage books themselves, of rural or even wilderness Reality Zones getting so strong, mundane technology is made to function less effectively, or not at all. As in, the Reality Zone doesn't just affect magickal Effects, but even Sleeper-tech. People expect it to be impossible to get a cell phone signal out in the woods, so the Consensus makes it so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-15-2019, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T11:47:38-08:00","id":1280368,"title":"","content":"I like to take an existing scene and tweak the contrast on it. Rather than having entire changes to Spheres, I look at a small subset and see how they could be different.<br /> <br /> Places:<br /> <b>Abandoned places:</b> Everything seems off kilter, not the same as the rest of the world. The mind starts to play tricks, an odd sense of being outside of time, the thing just lurking out of vision, decayed fragments that you can still barely recognize, the floor suddenly giving way underfoot. It helps that the Shroud is probably lower here too.<br /> <br /> <b>Californication:</b> Everyone is more beautiful, in better physical shape and more alive. Pride and lust run rampant. The home of Muscle Beach, porn studios and cosmetic surgery.<br /> <br /> <b>The endless halls/marketplace</b>: It's so easy for you to get lost and end up somewhere completely unexpected. Is it a feeling of paranoia or of freedom? <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/personal-log-of-gordon-richards\" target=\"_blank\">SCP 184</a> has a really great exploration of these themes.<br /> <br /> <b>Rural Chinese wu shu farms:</b> All the wuxia potential without any of the trouble Akashic meditation. Of course people can jump higher, break boards, that's what they train for! They have to look good for the movies.<br /> <br /> Events:<br /> <br /> <b>Burning Man</b>: Hot sun, dehydration, people throwing away inhibitions, weird devices. While not everything is possible that boundary is pushed a whole lot further back.<br /> <br /> <b>Magic shows/freak shows/Cirque du Soleil</b>: A select place and a select time when the impossible becomes possible and challenges people to explain how its done. People don't even need to know how things are really done, their explanation is enough to make it coincidental to themselves. Penn and Teller's Bullsh*t can provide some good examples. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=d_etsAX53Ys&amp;t=118s\" target=\"_blank\">The Sacred Riana</a> offers a Nephandic twist.<br /> <br /> Thank you for listening to my mumblings. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12228-spectrum","name":"Spectrum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-12T12:14:29-08:00","id":1280379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279128-using-reality-zones-examples?p=1279370#post1279370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, I vaguely recall mentions in the Mage books themselves, of rural or even wilderness Reality Zones getting so strong, mundane technology is made to function less effectively, or not at all. As in, the Reality Zone doesn't just affect magickal Effects, but even Sleeper-tech. People expect it to be impossible to get a cell phone signal out in the woods, so the Consensus makes it so.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is specifically mentioned as the effect of a reality zone covering the Empty Quarter of Arabia, a major Taftani stronghold (before M20 at least).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1410-czernobog","name":"Czernobog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-14T09:19:19-08:00","id":1280696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1279128-using-reality-zones-examples?p=1279370#post1279370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, I vaguely recall mentions in the Mage books themselves, of rural or even wilderness Reality Zones getting so strong, mundane technology is made to function less effectively, or not at all. As in, the Reality Zone doesn't just affect magickal Effects, but even Sleeper-tech. People expect it to be impossible to get a cell phone signal out in the woods, so the Consensus makes it so.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is stranger than that. The really remote zones- Primal Reality Zones- are stated to be in the most remote places of the world; untouched by people. There isn't much of a consensus to say anything one way or the other. The technology isn't failing because people expect it to fail, it is failing because there aren't enough people to expect it to succeed.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}